{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they observed the Passover in the first.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: according to the view of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, Israel did not observe the Passover in the wilderness except in this year alone, for they were unable to observe it because children and servants were born to them and they could not circumcise them, for the reason they mentioned — that it was a danger to them, as is explained in Yevamot. But in the Sifrei they said: ״ויעשו את הפסח בראשון״ — the verse speaks in criticism of Israel, that they observed only this Passover alone; and thus it says (Amos 5:25): ״הזבחים ומנחה הגשתם לי במדבר ארבעים שנה״. They derived this from this verse, which says ״ויעשו את הפסח בראשון בארבעה עשר במדבר סיני״, for it is a superfluous verse, since it would have been sufficient for it to say ״ויעשו את הפסח״ — 'and they observed the Passover' — ״ככל אשר צוה״; but it mentioned the day and the wilderness to hint that they observed it in the wilderness only on this day, and this is their criticism — end of his words. And the passage of the Passover was written here because the dedication of the altar was in the first month, and then the Levites were separated; and since it is written in the commandment of the Passover (Exodus 12:25): ״והיה כי תבאו אל הארץ״, and (Exodus 13:5): ״והיה כי יביאך״, He now commanded that they are obligated in it even in the wilderness."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:55.897081761Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}